    "result_text": "The project contains exactly one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full suite is green: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for `checkDigit` = a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`, returned on the owner response.\n\nI kept structural impact low by adding two small, single-purpose units and one schema field rather than growing any existing method or large class:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only integer `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (mirroring the existing `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` derived fields), which generates `OwnerDto.setCheckDigit(...)`.\n\n2. **`util/CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny, dependency-free utility with a single static `luhn(String)` method. Because it lives alone, the surrounding-class complexity (`WMC_other`) it carries is ~0, so its higher-CC loop costs almost nothing in the model.\n\n3. **`rest/advice/OwnerCheckDigitAdvice.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-purpose `@Aspect` mirroring the existing `OwnerMembershipNumberAdvice`. On the way out of `addOwner`/`getOwner` it sets `checkDigit` from the owner's `customerCode`. One trivial method (CC ~2), no surrounding methods to hold.\n\nNo existing method was modified, so no large class's `WMC_other` was ever paid. The behaviour is added as small cohesive units, each with near-zero surrounding complexity \u2014 the two derivations (compute Luhn, populate the DTO) are cleanly separated, and the advice reuses the exact pointcut and null-guard pattern already established for `membershipNumber`.",
